# Encryption and keys

Field-level encryption
- Implemented via prisma-field-encryption annotations in app/prisma/schema.prisma (/// @encrypted and hash annotations)
- Generated helpers in app/prisma/reencrypt/* (index.ts per-model migrators)
- Sensitive fields include User.email/password, AccountRegister.name/plaid fields/walletAddress, RegisterEntry.description/plaidId, Reoccurrence.description, etc.

Re-encryption after restore
- docs/post-restore-encryption-plan.md describes the local-restore strategy
- scripts/dump-and-restore.sh invokes scripts/reset-encrypted-users-after-restore.ts to sanitize or re-encrypt data
- Strategy supports:
  - Using source env key + local key to re-encrypt via generated migrate() where available
  - Fallback placeholder overwrites for sensitive fields when source key is absent

Key rotation (staging)
- .deploy/key-rotation-cronjob.template.yaml schedules nightly append-only DB key rotation
- Cron container uses microservice Docker image target runner-keyrotate and runs scripts/k8s-rotate-db-key.sh to update secrets and restart Deployments, then triggers microservice migration endpoint
- RBAC in .deploy/key-rotation-rbac.template.yaml must be applied with appropriate permissions

Do/do not
- Do not log decrypted values or keys
- Keep DATABASE_URL and DB_ENCRYPTION_KEY out of code; inject via Kubernetes secrets or .env locally
- When adding new encrypted fields, ensure annotations exist in schema; run prisma generate to refresh reencrypt code
